# @jsr packages only exist on JSR's npm gateway; registry.npmjs.org 404s for
# the scope. Declared at the workspace root so every pnpm invocation in this
# repo routes the scope correctly — including the supply-chain verification
# pass pnpm 11+ runs against the whole lockfile: it re-fetches each entry's
# packument from the registry the scope routes to and hard-fails on a 404
# (ERR_PNPM_META_FETCH_FAIL). A sub-package .npmrc is invisible to
# workspace-root installs, which is what broke CI when pnpm's latest tag
# moved to 12.
#
# Also do not reintroduce a sub-package .npmrc: a `pnpm -r publish` child for
# a package that has its own .npmrc uses that file instead of the workspace
# root file, so it hides the root file's auth token from the npm child the
# publish spawns (ENEEDAUTH). The package-e2e publish script writes its
# localhost token to this file; verified 2026-09-07 with a stub registry.
@jsr:registry=https://npm.jsr.io/
